<Project>

  <!--
    MSBuild imports only the NEAREST Directory.Build.props walking up from a csproj, so this file
    shadows the repo's root one. Import that first or every app in this folder silently loses
    $(Version), $(VhDir) and $(VhUserDir) — and the heads embed their private appsettings and their
    default access key from $(VhUserDir), so they would build green and ship with neither.
  -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!--
    NO APP IS EVER A NUGET PACKAGE.

    pub/lib/Publish-NugetPackages.ps1 discovers what to publish by packing every project under src/
    that has not opted out, so a head that forgets the opt-out ships to nuget.org as a library. That
    is not hypothetical: the iOS app and its network extension were missing it and were published as
    vpnhood.app.client.ios, vpnhood.app.client.ios.extension and vpnhood.app.connect.ios, up to
    8.1.845.8, each with a dependency on projects that are not packages at all.

    Sixteen per-project copies of one line could not hold that rule, because the seventeenth head is
    written by someone who did not know it existed. This covers the folder and everything added to
    it. The per-project lines stay as the local statement of the same fact.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
